      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "Python confirms seq[119]='T' and seq[120]='G', consistent with 'Thr-120' in the paper; insert_after_residue=120 places the tag between T120 and G121 within EC loop C (residues 116\u2013135). Minimum distance from TM boundaries is 5 residues (TM3 ends at 115). The paper explicitly demonstrates exofacial topology by protease digestion of intact oocytes, providing direct experimental confirmation. No N-glycosylation sequon is disrupted at this position. Coronavirus E1 glycoprotein epitope inserted at Thr-120 of full-length CHIP/AQP1 expressed in Xenopus oocytes. Topology confirmed exofacial by alpha-chymotrypsin digestion of intact oocytes (protease-sensitive), placing the epitope on the extracellular face of loop C (EC span 116\u2013135). [validation: surface_only; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 7507481,
          "citation": "PMID 7507481",
          "claim": "An epitope from the coronavirus E1 glycoprotein was inserted into CHIP and localized to the outer or inner leaflet of the membrane by alpha-chymotrypsin digestion of intact oocytes or inside-out membrane vesicles. The E1 epitope at Thr-120 was protease-sensitive in intact oocytes, indicating that loop C is exofacial. The E1 epitope at Lys-6, Arg-162, or Lys-267 was protease-sensitive in inside-out membrane vesicles, confirming the cytoplasmic location of the NH2 and COOH termini and loop D."
        }
      ],
