      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "Python confirms seq[42]='Q' and seq[43]='T', placing the junction squarely within EC loop A (residues 34\u201349). Minimum distance from TM boundaries is 7 residues (TM2 starts at 50). Four independent publications (L1\u2013L4) all name this exact Gln43\u2013Thr44 junction, making it the best-evidenced site in the ledger. A potential N-glycosylation sequon N42-Q43-T44 is disrupted by the insertion, but all four papers demonstrate successful surface trafficking of the tagged protein, so this is not a blocking concern. FLAG epitope inserted between Gln43 and Thr44 in extracellular loop A (EC span 34\u201349) of full-length AQP1 expressed in mammalian cells. Reported independently in four ledger lines (L1\u2013L4), covering LSAqp1, hAQP1, and an Aqp1-FKBP12-DD fusion. Surface detection performed with anti-FLAG antibodies on non-permeabilized cells. [validation: surface_only; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
