  "literature_notes": "Five ledger lines were evaluated. L1, L2, L3, and L4 all independently pin the identical Gln43\u2013Thr44 junction in EC loop A; L2 was chosen as the primary supporting clip for Site 1 (hAQP1, most direct), but all four corroborate it. L5 pins a second distinct site at Thr-120 in EC loop C. The cytoplasmic sites from L5 (Lys-6, Arg-162, Lys-267) were excluded because they are intracellular and the paper itself confirms this by protease sensitivity on inside-out vesicles only. EC loop 3 (residues 187\u2013210) contains no ledger-supported insertion and was not proposed. No terminal sites were proposed because both termini of AQP1 are intracellular (confirmed by topology landmarks and by the papers themselves, which explicitly state this as the reason for inserting into an extracellular loop).",
